      "worked": "The base $AB$ lies on the $x$-axis and has length $10-5=5\\text{ cm}$. Let $h$ be the perpendicular height.\n$$\\begin{align*}20&=\\tfrac12\\times5\\times h\\\\h&=\\frac{2\\times20}{5}\\\\h&=8\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $C$ must be 8 cm above or below the $x$-axis. Its $y$-coordinate is $8$ or $-8$, and its $x$-coordinate can be any number.",
